# Approval Detail — Production Crash Prevention

## Canonical route

One helper contract only:

`/app/approvals?request=<approval-uuid>`

- Helpers: `buildApprovalsDeepLink`, `resolveApprovalDetailHref`, `selectFocusedApprovalId`, `resolveEccApprovalNavigationHref` in `lib/companion-action-approval/parse.ts`
- Exact CORE `action_requests.id` UUID in the URL
- Tenant resolved server-side from session — never from URL org params

## Navigation (mandatory)

- When an approval UUID exists in `href` / `record_href` / `approval_id`, **never rewrite** the CTA to bare `/app/command-center/approvals`
- Client `canAccessApprovals` / profile-loading must not drop the UUID (decision auth stays server-side)
- While dashboard profile is loading, treat approvals deep links as keepable — do not assume denied
- ECC, Approval Center, Kompis, and notifications must share the same approval ID

## Loader

- Normalize with `normalizeApprovalDetail()` — null description, expires_at, actor, and optional binding fields must not throw
- Website Kompis publish/rollback: show path, locale, candidate, versions, checksum/audit when present
- Incomplete binding → controlled “cannot process” state + disabled decisions — never crash
- Historical / wrong-tenant / missing → controlled state — never English `global-error`

## Error UI

- Approval detail and ECC segments must have localized `error.tsx` boundaries
- Never rely on English `app/global-error.tsx` for approval detail failures
- Actions: retry, back to approvals, back to Kompis when relevant
- Technical digest only inside a details section — no raw stacks/secrets/full UUID as primary copy

## Decisions

Approve/Reject only when: found, tenant match, actionable pending, binding complete (website), checksum present, not expired/cancelled/consumed/emergency.

## Forbidden

- UnoNight hardcoding in Core
- Browser/session/MFA handling in this surface
- Live approval decision, publish, or rollback inside repair tasks
